{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":42.4900016784668,"text":"In 1806, Napoleon had just won a great battle and ordered an enormous arch so that his soldiers could march home underneath it. Building it took thirty years, far longer than his own rule lasted, and Napoleon never saw it finished. The arch is fifty meters high, about the height of a sixteen-story building, and hundreds of names of battles and generals are carved into its walls. It stands in the middle of a square from which twelve avenues run out like spokes, which is why from above it looks like a star. Under the arch lies the grave of a soldier who was never identified, and beside it a flame that has been lit every evening since 1923 and has never gone out.","words":[{"word":"In","start":0,"end":0.47999998927116394},{"word":"1806","start":0.47999998927116394,"end":1.6200000047683716},{"word":"Napoleon","start":2.180000066757202,"end":2.180000066757202},{"word":"had","start":2.180000066757202,"end":2.5199999809265137},{"word":"just","start":2.5199999809265137,"end":2.940000057220459},{"word":"won","start":2.940000057220459,"end":3.0199999809265137},{"word":"a","start":3.0199999809265137,"end":3.1600000858306885},{"word":"great","start":3.1600000858306885,"end":3.440000057220459},{"word":"battle","start":3.440000057220459,"end":3.700000047683716},{"word":"and","start":3.700000047683716,"end":4.320000171661377},{"word":"ordered","start":4.320000171661377,"end":4.579999923706055},{"word":"an","start":4.579999923706055,"end":4.880000114440918},{"word":"enormous","start":4.880000114440918,"end":5.440000057220459},{"word":"arch","start":5.440000057220459,"end":5.760000228881836},{"word":"so","start":5.760000228881836,"end":6.21999979019165},{"word":"that","start":6.21999979019165,"end":6.420000076293945},{"word":"his","start":6.420000076293945,"end":6.699999809265137},{"word":"soldiers","start":6.699999809265137,"end":6.880000114440918},{"word":"could","start":6.880000114440918,"end":7.2399997